WEBVTT

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.830
He fell!

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.060
Playmaker!

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.190
We're falling we're falling we're falling!

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.170
What?

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.110
They're back.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.650
Did you do this?

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.840
Huh?  Of course not.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.580
Then what did I sense?

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.550
More importantly, look at that.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.320
The third level is complete.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.440
If we don't hurry, major trouble.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.180
When the sixth level is completed, it's over.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.260
Let's go!

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.730
Playmaker is entering the 
Tower of Hanoi alone?

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.510
Since we've come this far, we'll 
report from LINK VRAINS to the end!

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.480
Right!

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.720
Don't stop filming even if 
we're turned into particles!

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.490
Okay!

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.720
I run Across the universe

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:31.890
At the speed of light

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.760
Begin Loading

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:37.490
Open the door of dreams

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:41.060
VRAINS spreads

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.170
Believe in myself

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.700
VRAINS continues

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:53.010
The circuit draws the future

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.080
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.680
Access!

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.380
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:02.980
I'm now With the Wind

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.290
Link with my soul

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.060
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.790
Now Win the Race

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.630
Connected world

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:16.130
No matter when

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.500
Nothing is impossible

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.640
Strive for hope

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.210
And ride the wind!

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.270
As your manager, I can't 
let you go to LINK VRAINS.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.740
You can't stop me.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.180
Because you're fired.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.000
So you're going, no matter what.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.180
Thanks for everything.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.690
Then make me one promise.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.650
Promise to come back.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.170
Who ya think you're talking to?

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.670
I'm Go Onizuka!

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.600
I will return.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.980
I can't let you go any further.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:56.520
Are you Revolver?

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:59.520
You're Go Onizuka.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.990
You're using that tower 
to destroy everything.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.960
What's your goal?

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.210
What's the point of discussing that?

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:15.670
You have no intention of 
understanding our goal.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.180
That's true.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.910
I won't listen to the nonsense of a villain!

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.740
Villain?

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.510
Well, I guess I appear like a villain.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.980
Silence!  No matter your cause, 
this can't be forgiven!

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:36.970
But you shouldn't have come here.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.740
The Tower of Hanoi absorbed Blue Angel.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:44.930
If you don't want that 
to happen to you, leave.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.900
What?  Blue Angel?

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.510
My subordinate Spectre defeated her.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:57.010
But Playmaker defeated Spectre.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.380
My opponent is Playmaker, not you.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.750
Stop playing!

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:08.720
If Playmaker defeated your 
subordinate, then I'll defeat you!

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.020
Oh well then.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:15.200
You have the skill to defeat 
Hanoi's three knights.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.400
Since you insist, I'll duel you!

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.410
So arrogant.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.400
Playmaker said...

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:28.150
Revolver has a terrifying card.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:34.120
But I powered up my Gouki 
Deck for a new duel!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.080
Let's go!

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.860
Duel!

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.600
I go first!  It's my turn!

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.900
I summon Gouki Suprex from my hand!

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:06.180
When it's summoned, I can Special 
Summon Gouki Twistcobra!

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.600
Appear!  My circuit!

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.130
The summoning conditions are two Goukis!

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:21.300
I set Gouki Twistcobra and 
Suprex in the Link Markers!

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.030
Link Summon!

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:27.970
Appear, Link 2 Gouki Jet Ogre!

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:31.460
Since Gouki Suprex and Twistcobra were sent from

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:34.940
the field to the graveyard, their effects activate!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:39.920
I add two other Gouki cards 
from my deck to my hand!

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:44.310
Look at that!

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:45.850
It's a duel!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.340
Hey, Playmaker!

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.120
Someone's dueling over there.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.410
Seriously?

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.860
Since Blue Angel and Spectre 
are gone, it must be...

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.330
Go Onizuka and Revolver.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.780
It's dangerous here.  You should leave.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.800
No, can't do that!

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:14.550
We know you're risking your 
lives to protect LINK VRAINS.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.240
So we'll also risk our lives for the truth-

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.720
He left.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:23.940
Stop dawdling!  Go after him!

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.490
Okay!

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:27.090
I'm not done!

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.840
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Gouki Re-Match!

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:37.940
I Special Summon two Goukis with different 
Levels from my graveyard in defense position!

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:43.010
Appear again!  My circuit!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.120
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Goukis!

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.760
I set Gouki Suprex and Link 2 Jet Ogre!

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.820
Link Summon!

00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:01.780
Appear, Link 3 Gouki Thunder Ogre!

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.600
Thunder Ogre's effect!

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:12.610
As long as it's in the Monster 
Zone, I can summon again!

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:16.980
I call Gouki Suprex!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:25.810
When Suprex is summoned, I can Special 
Summon Riscorpio from my hand!

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.200
I end my turn.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:41.010
He's full of vigor!

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.940
Revolver...

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:48.180
You're too late, Playmaker.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:51.660
I'll be the one to defeat Revolver.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.910
Stay quiet and watch!

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:57.780
Distracted by a bystander 
when you're facing me?

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:59.920
You must be very confident.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.380
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.200
Start the broadcast!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.090
Put your heart into it!

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:17.910
Okay!

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:22.380
Go Onizuka vs Revolver?  Yusaku is there too!

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:27.350
Do whatever it takes to stop the 
Tower of Hanoi from being built!

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.150
Hey!  It's Onizuka!

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.940
Beat that Knight of Hanoi!

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.620
Good luck!

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:42.860
So this is why Onizuka hasn't been around...

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.330
Go will return.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:48.300
Let's believe in him.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:49.850
Yes.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:57.890
When there's a Link Monster on your field, I 
can Special Summon Gateway Dragon from my hand.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:04.360
Gateway Dragon's effect activates.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:10.190
I Special Summon one Level 4 or 
lower Dark Dragon from my hand.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:13.190
Come out, Sniffer Dragon!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:18.200
When it's summoned or Special Summoned...

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:24.380
...I can add another Sniffer Dragon 
from my deck to my hand and summon it.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:29.250
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:33.950
The summoning conditions are at 
least two non-Token monsters.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:40.580
I set Gateway Dragon and two Sniffer 
Dragons in the Link Markers!

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.850
Link Summon!

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:51.310
Appear, Link 3 Triple Burst Dragon!

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.870
2400 ATK...

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:59.340
But I can strike back using 
Gouki Twistcobra's effect.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:05.580
When there are monsters with the same number 
of Link Markers in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:09.950
...from my hand, I can activate 
the spell card, Arrow Charge!

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:12.120
I draw two cards.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:14.890
And we both can look at them.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:18.770
And now, Gouki Thunder Ogre's effect!

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:25.720
I can summon a monster on my field 
next to Thunder Ogre's link!

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.120
Come, Triggering Wurm*!

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:34.690
I used your monster's effect to my advantage.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:37.880
Link 4 is coming!

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.850
Manifest!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:45.550
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters!

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:52.360
I set Triggering Wurm and Link 3 Triple 
Burst Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.000
Link Summon!

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:06.260
Appear, Link 4 Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.280
Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:17.990
That's one of Revolver's ace monsters.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:20.950
Triggering Wurm's effect activates.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:26.420
When I use it to Link Summon 
Topologic Bomber Dragon...

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:31.140
...I can Special Summon Triggering Wurm 
from my graveyard next to its link.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:36.770
Topologic Bomber Dragon's effect activates!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.240
This feels bad!

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:44.650
When a different monster is Special 
Summoned next to a Link Monster's link...

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:48.780
...all monsters in our Main 
Monster Zones are destroyed!

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:50.530
Full Overlap!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.840
In that case, I activate 
Gouki Twistcobra's effect!

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:58.420
I tribute Riscorpio.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:04.430
Thunder Ogre gains 2300 ATK 
until the end of the turn!

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:22.950
When a Link Monster's effect destroys 
Triggering Wurm, I draw one card from my deck.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.180
Only the Main Monster Zones were destroyed.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.340
Thunder Ogre was in the Extra Monster Zone!

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:32.660
Thunder Ogre's effect activates!

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:39.140
When an effect destroys a monster 
next to its link, it gains 400 ATK!

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:42.840
And since Gouki Suprex, Twistcobra and Riscorpio

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.600
were sent to the graveyard, their effects activate!

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:50.590
I add three Gouki cards 
in my deck to my hand.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.330
This fight is only getting started!

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:56.110
He's trying really hard!

00:13:56.790 --> 00:14:01.760
From my hand, I activate the 
Continuous Spell, Link Protection!

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:08.000
Topologic Bomber can't be 
destroyed in battle this turn...

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:11.460
...and we both take 0 battle damage.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:14.940
Go, Topologic Bomber Dragon.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:18.410
Attack Gouki Thunder Ogre!

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:28.950
What?  It's pointless to attack 
if you can't destroy it!

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:33.680
And when the battle ends, 
your monster is destroyed!

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.760
Ah.  I see.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:46.210
Topologic Bomber Dragon's effect activates.

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:50.710
You take damage equal to 
your monster's original ATK.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:53.670
Aiming Blast!

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.790
I activate Gouki Octostretch's 
effect from my hand!

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:04.980
By discarding this card, damage is halved!

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:12.140
Nice!  Keep it up!

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.820
Watch quietly!

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:14.740
Fine.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.560
Not bad.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:22.770
But how long will it last?

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:26.500
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:36.940
Just wait, everyone!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.090
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:45.590
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Gouki Re-Match!

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:50.090
I Special Summon two Goukis 
in defense position!

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:55.130
I promise to restore LINK VRAINS!

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:58.370
Appear!  My circuit!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.350
The summoning conditions are two Goukis!

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:07.310
I set Gouki Suprex and Twistcobra 
in the Link Markers!

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.820
Link Summon!

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:16.020
Appear, Link 2 Gouki Shadow Ogre!

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:27.000
If a monster is Special Summoned next 
to Topologic Bomber Dragon's link...

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:31.450
...all monsters in our Main 
Monster Zones will be destroyed.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:35.310
Exactly.  And it's guaranteed to activate.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.380
What are you planning?

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:42.250
You're about to find out!

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.060
Gouki Shadow Ogre's effect activates!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:52.960
Since Topologic Bomber is next to its link, 
Toplogic Bomber's effect is negated and destroyed!

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:54.500
What?

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.780
Yeah!  He destroyed Topologic!

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:15.990
He did it!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:21.320
I also used your monster's 
effect to my advantage.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:30.360
Due to Shadow Ogre's effect, I can Special 
Summon a Gouki Link Monster from my graveyard.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:34.270
I call Gouki Thunder Ogre!

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:40.700
And since Gouki Suprex and Twistcobra 
were sent to the graveyard...

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:44.680
...I add two Gouki cards 
in my deck to my hand!

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:47.920
Now Go Onizuka has two Link Monsters.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:50.920
And he's still allowed to Normal Summon.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.390
And he has six cards in his hand!

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.850
Probably full of Gouki monsters.

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:59.590
But why is he confident?

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:04.310
The Continuous Spell Link Protection's 
additional effect activates.

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:09.680
By banishing this card and the destroyed 
Topologic Bomber from my graveyard...

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.750
...unless you have at least the same number of

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:16.420
Link Monsters as my banished monster's Link Markers...

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:18.850
...you can't attack this turn.

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:21.590
Topologic is Link 4.

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:26.590
That means he can't attack unless 
he has four Link Monsters.

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:32.520
How clever.  Then I just 
need to get two more!

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:36.180
I summon Gouki Suprex from my hand!

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:44.110
Due to Suprex's effect, I Special 
Summon Gouki Riscorpio from my hand!

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:48.610
And I activate Gouki Headbatt's 
effect from my hand!

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:54.820
I send one Gouki monster in my hand to the 
graveyard to Special Summon it in defense position!

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.120
Next is Headbatt's effect!

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:02.990
Thunder Ogre gains 800 ATK 
until the end of the turn!

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.990
Appear!  My circuit!

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:12.170
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Goukis.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:18.160
I set Gouki Suprex, Riscorpio and 
Headbatt in the Link Markers!

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:23.470
Link Summon!

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:29.780
Appear, Link 3 Gouki The Great Ogre!

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.660
Just one more...

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:41.130
Since Riscorpio and Headbatt were sent 
to the graveyard, their effects activate!

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:44.860
I add two Gouki cards in my deck to my hand!

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:48.270
Next is the Continuous Spell, Gouki Shout!

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:57.340
When my Gouki attacks, it gains 300 ATK 
for every Gouki monster on my field!

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:04.880
And from my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Gouki Face Turn!

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:10.260
I destroy Gouki Shout to Special 
Summon a monster from the graveyard!

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.010
Resurrect, Gouki Jet Ogre!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:20.070
All right!  Now he has four Link Monsters!

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:23.270
Hey, why are you so depressing?

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:26.870
He'll attack him repeatedly and win.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.100
No...

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.700
That!

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:41.320
I promised to protect LINK VRAINS 
so the children would smile!

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:47.320
That's why I, Go Onizuka, will defeat you!

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:52.130
I don't hate passionate people like you.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.100
But I'm cold-hearted in a duel.

00:20:55.380 --> 00:21:00.430
Battle!  Great Ogre attacks you directly!

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:05.050
Sink into the abyss of bottomless despair!

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.480
What's this light?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.600
This light is...

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:25.530
I activate the trap card, Mirror Force.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:30.000
All your monsters in attack 
position are destroyed!

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:39.610
What?

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:53.360
The terrifying card that Playmaker 
mentioned was Mirror Force!

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.690
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:22.830
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:30.030
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:37.410
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:44.620
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:45.020 --> 00:22:48.790
There were fragments of power

00:22:49.020 --> 00:22:55.960
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:03.300
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.430 --> 00:23:10.510
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:17.710
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:24.590
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:32.260
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:42.020
Mirror Force was enough to fire up Onizuka.

00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:46.470
The battle's now to see who is the strongest.

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:54.490
When his fighting spirit breaks the chains 
that bind him, his hidden power is released!

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:58.410
This won't be enough to break him.

00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:02.790
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Thirst for Victory

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:05.090
Into the VRAINS!
